From 8aca880b290c5c667ce87a5be68a61be1e55f038 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 22:22:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 183/225] feat: specular and emissive atlas layers in the RT
 material record

Stage 2B of the rt plan. A ray traced hit now carries the same four material
maps the primary surface does, so hit shading (2A) can use CE's own
reflectance and emittance instead of an albedo-only approximation.

- FillRTMaterialRecord requests EFTT_SPECULAR and EFTT_EMITTANCE low-res
  copies through the same CheckStoreTextureInPool path as albedo and normal:
  refcounted atlas slices, the same BC1..BC7 restriction (anything else
  returns no slice and the material keeps slot 0), the same per-cell release.
  matInfo0.y = ExtractUint2(normal+1, specular+1), matInfo0.z =
  ExtractUint2(emissive+1, 0), matching decision 02 section 2.5 and the
  consumer in CommonSVO_RT.cfi RT_ProcessBestHit.

- matInfo1.y (specular reflectance) = the unweighted channel average of
  GetColorValue(EFTT_SPECULAR), which is REG_PM_SPECULAR_COL = MatSpecColor.rgb,
  exactly what Illum.cfx uses for attribs.Reflectance before multiplying the
  specular map. The record has no room for a coloured F0, so a coloured metal
  loses its tint; documented in the report.

- matInfo1.w (emissive) = the RAW kcd/m2 value, i.e.
  GetFinalEmittance().Luminance() / (1000 / RENDERER_LIGHT_UNIT_SCALE).
  Illum.cfx computes MatEmissiveColor.rgb * MatEmissiveColor.w *
  MAT_EMISSIVE_UNIT_SCALE, and MAT_EMISSIVE_UNIT_SCALE is literally
  1000/10000 - the same factor GetFinalEmittance already applies. The
  consumer applies it, so the producer divides it back out; a reflected
  emissive surface is then the same brightness as the surface itself.

- The emissive atlas copy folds Illum's GetEmittanceMask into the alpha
  (luminance(rgb) * a), which is the single channel the consumer reads.
  EmittanceMapGamma is not applied - no room in the record.

- Known gap 7.2 is kept but no longer silent: a material whose normal,
  specular or emissive copy has a different size than its albedo copy is
  counted and warned about once per level (the record carries one UV scale).

- The self test gains a material record round trip over six slot
  combinations (including 0 = no map and the 4095 field limit), checking the
  specular and emissive slots, the ExtractUint2 padding and the atlas UV
  scale against the consumer's decoders.

